#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115392 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114972 :question/id #uuid "cbb15346-028c-59c0-9b20-cd2f408c3bcb" :question/math-academy-id "e-2479" :question/problem "Find $(\\mathbf f \\circ u)'(t),$ if $\\mathbf f(u) = \\ln u \\, \\mathbf i + (u^2+5) \\, \\mathbf j + 4u \\, \\mathbf k$ and $u(t) =2t^3.$" :question/worked-solution "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(\\mathbf f \\circ u)'(t) = \\mathbf{f}'(u(t)) u'(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivative of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡u)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({u}^{2}+5)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(4u)k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\,i+2u\\,j+4\\,k, \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3})=6{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{u(t)}\\,i+2u(t)\\,j+4\\,k){u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2{t}^{3}}\\,i+2(2{t}^{3})\\,j+4\\,k)\\cdot 6{t}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{t}\\,i+24{t}^{5}\\,j+24{t}^{2}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a146d5d3-2562-5b8b-886e-4cf6519d3282" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051084 :topic/math-academy-id 1108 :topic/title "The Chain Rule for Differentiation"}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552750 :question-generator/id #uuid "cf1b3915-9b3c-50c7-be1e-3ec2338b67dd" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186115392.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115767 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "041da615-473a-59b3-bd74-078cc5cac382" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8t+8 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299946} {:answer/id #uuid "278a088d-66ff-5fc3-9def-6ae04de020b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4t+4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300150} {:answer/id #uuid "67ce37ea-b2ab-5a58-86f8-69d3f8240639" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8t \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300484} {:answer/id #uuid "ab0ec50a-1d0e-532d-ab8d-7cf840b59340" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2t \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300820} {:answer/id #uuid "f2329096-2544-59c2-a74f-b394b5ad02bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4t+4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301157}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "041da615-473a-59b3-bd74-078cc5cac382" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8t+8 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299946} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1a16360-6703-53e1-9901-03f44bb4aa65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301808}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0fd1def5-bd75-572c-939f-770f964a1db9" :question/math-academy-id "q-32498" :question/problem "If $f(u)=\\begin{bmatrix}2u \\\\ {u}^{2} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $u(t)=2t+2$, then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(2u) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\,({u}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(3)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2u \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t+2)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & =f′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2u(t) \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2(2t+2) \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8t+8 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115772 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "889f8013-9633-5472-a777-eca4c5e41e7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3{t}^{2}\\,i-6{t}^{2}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303308} {:answer/id #uuid "905a9185-fbd2-5d1d-b551-1887761f23f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{3}\\,i-6{t}^{5}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303358} {:answer/id #uuid "a284a409-3695-5062-bf15-c301f1626b27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{3}\\,i-2{t}^{5}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303458} {:answer/id #uuid "d627a4e8-bf07-5d84-bdda-4e0a8ab4c680" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,i-2u\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303786} {:answer/id #uuid "fd4b1cc6-899c-5984-bb4f-022c7fed3343" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{3}\\,i-6{t}^{3}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "905a9185-fbd2-5d1d-b551-1887761f23f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{3}\\,i-6{t}^{5}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303358} :answer-field/id #uuid "1317e8fd-c944-52dc-90c8-a38a479a2646" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304116}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6d41b7e5-385e-5e64-81bc-3cb7a2474527" :question/math-academy-id "q-32866" :question/problem "If $f(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,i+(1-{u}^{2})\\,j+12\\,k$ and $u(t)={t}^{3}$ then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(1-{u}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(12)\\,k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,i-2u\\,j+0\\,k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,i-2u\\,j \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})=3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(u(t))\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u(t))\\,i-2(u(t))\\,j)\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{3})\\,i-2({t}^{3})\\,j)\\cdot 3{t}^{2} \\\\  & =-3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{3}\\,i-6{t}^{5}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262923 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22d174aa-f9dc-519a-9e06-114c43894f47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,t{sec}^{2}⁡({t}^{2})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260180} {:answer/id #uuid "3661956c-4318-53fc-ab1c-41b76ef2b5bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260361} {:answer/id #uuid "3e0b2ee6-a1be-5aa4-868f-eda5b7d48d90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,2t{cos}^{2}⁡({t}^{2})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260421} {:answer/id #uuid "d905812a-aaa1-5520-a293-216f1bd217d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t\\operatorname{sec}⁡({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261788} {:answer/id #uuid "fe28d3f4-7453-5eff-b63a-74f22f763357" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{2}{t},\\,2t{sec}^{2}⁡({t}^{2})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262104}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe28d3f4-7453-5eff-b63a-74f22f763357" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2